From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:33:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] strip scanout from a P010 buffer the host cannot scan out

A 10-bit buffer that the composer may show (GPU texture, composer overlay
and video decoder usage together) was refused as an unsupported
combination, because only NV12 and the RGB formats lost the scanout flag
when the host cannot scan them out. The codec waited for a block for good,
and a decoder that produced P010 surfaces timed out.

P010 now loses the scanout flag the same way, and the GPU composes the
buffer.
---
 virtgpu_virgl.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/virtgpu_virgl.c b/virtgpu_virgl.c
index 6b6d10d2e846d9fa31011aec85915433cdf6f0ef..e6695a7a276f64e006c8f8706ec0d6fc1d1ebcac 100644
--- a/virtgpu_virgl.c
+++ b/virtgpu_virgl.c
@@ -1412,6 +1412,7 @@ static void virgl_3d_resolve_format_and_use_flags(struct driver *drv, uint32_t f
 	/* resolve explicit format */
 	switch (*out_format) {
 	case DRM_FORMAT_NV12:
+	case DRM_FORMAT_P010:
 	case DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888:
 	case DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888:
 	case DRM_FORMAT_RGB565:
